 "result": "The decorator is `needs_app_scope`, and the class that loads the app is `LaunchInfo`. This repo is a renamed Flask, so these correspond to Flask's `with_appcontext` and `ScriptInfo`.\n\n- **Decorator:** `needs_app_scope`, at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and pushes `app.app_context()` around your callback.\n  - You usually don't need to write it yourself. Commands registered with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()` already get the app context (`app.py:338`, `bundles.py:49`).\n  - A standalone `AppGroup` (`cli.py:405`) wraps its `.command()` callbacks in it automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n- **Loader:** `LaunchInfo.load_app()`, at `src/tessel/cli.py:333`. It uses `create_app` or `--app` / `TESSEL_APP`, falling back to `wsgi.py` or `app.py`. Access it in a command with `pass_script_info` (`cli.py:375`).\n- **Top-level group:** `TesselGroup` (`cli.py:531`).\n\nDocs are in `docs/cli.rst`, around line 346.",
